  ## Concurrent Sentences:
  Certain crimes of a similar nature, listed below and indicated by sharing a colour on the Quick Crime Guide, should have their sentences carried out concurrently; their duration should not be added together. For more information, refer to [textlink="Sentencing" link="SpaceLaw"].

  1. Contraband crimes of any tier.

  2. Endangerment, Manslaughter, Murder, and Mass Murder.

  3. Assault and Major Assault.

  4. Disturbance, Rioting, and Sedition.

  5. Vandalism, Destruction of Property, and Mass Destruction.

  6. Trespass and Secure Trespass.

  7. Petty Theft and Grand Theft.

  8. Petty Fraud and Fraud.

  # Full Crime List
  Sentence durations are indicated in minutes. W indicates a Warning, P indicates Permanent confinement, E indicates Execution.

  ## Tier 1
  Tier 1 crimes are typically minor misbehaviours that can be disruptive to a safe and productive workplace environment. First-time offenders are recommended to be issued a stern warning so that they may promptly resume work.

  Fines for tier 1 crimes are not to exceed a maximum of 30 credits.
